          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<h2>Why heat and moisture kill probiotics</h2><p>Probiotics are living organisms. Like all living things, they're vulnerable to their environment. Heat speeds up cellular metabolism, eventually causing cell death. Moisture wakes dormant cultures prematurely, exhausting their energy reserves before they reach your gut. Combine the two — typical of a delivery truck in South African summer — and a probiotic capsule can lose half its potency in weeks.</p><p>This is why most conventional probiotics require refrigeration. And why most conventional probiotics fail anyway — by the time they're shipped from manufacturer to pharmacy to your kitchen, the cold chain has been broken multiple times.</p>"
